/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  layoutDict -- the PLOT PLAN of the apalutamide tablet plant (DEV.md 4c C97,
  phase A).  A STARTING POINT for the group, to copy and change.

  HOW IT WAS MADE.  `bin/choupo-layout --draft` placed the four items whose
  sizers publish a diameter and a height (the spray dryer and three
  vessels) on one line; it was then arranged by hand into a SOLVENT AREA
  east of the buildings and a TANK AREA south of the pipe rack, with the
  site buildings as NON-PROCESS items.

  THE SITE, west to east, with the prevailing wind FROM THE WEST (below):
    * the offices and the quality-control laboratory, and the gate;
    * the WAREHOUSE (raw materials in quarantine, released materials, the
      packed product awaiting release);
    * the GMP PRODUCTION BUILDING: dispensing, blending, roller
      compaction, milling, final blending, tableting, film coating and
      packaging all happen INSIDE it.  None of those machines is a sized
      item (they are mass-balance placeholders in the flowsheet), so the
      plot plan sees the building as ONE declared box; ITS INTERIOR -- rooms,
      cleanliness grades, the pressure cascade, the flows of people,
      material and waste -- is the `building {}` block at the end of this
      file, whose `envelope` is that box;
    * the SOLVENT AREA, downwind: the solution tank, the spray dryer and its
      closed nitrogen loop (heater, blower, exhaust cooler, condenser,
      condensate pot), with the acetone tanks south of the rack.  Everything
      that holds acetone is out here, away from people and from ignition
      sources, and its hazardous-area zones are declared.

  WHAT IS THE ENGINE'S AND WHAT IS OURS.  The spray dryer's chamber and the
  three vessels' diameters and heights are their sizers' own; the
  exchangers, the blower and the tanks publish an AREA, a POWER or a
  VOLUME, not a shape, so their plan boxes are DECLARED below (each with
  the arithmetic).  EVERYTHING ELSE IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION FOR THE
  GROUP TO REPLACE WITH ITS OWN SITE DATA: every position, every building's
  size, every separation distance, the wind and every hazardous-area zone.
  They are round numbers chosen so that the checks are visible on this
  plant, not values from any spacing or hazardous-area standard: the
  published ones (IEC 60079-10-1 and its national codes for zones; company
  and insurance spacing guides) grant no redistribution, and a citation
  invented for a round number would turn "unsourced" into "falsely sourced".

  ONE FINDING IS LEFT ON PURPOSE: the coating-suspension tank stands 4 m
  from the production building, inside the 15 m the separation table asks
  between a `vessel` and a building.  The check reads the equipment KIND,
  not what the vessel holds -- this one holds a water suspension of a
  polymer and pigments, nothing that burns.  The group must either justify
  the distance or, better, put the tank where it belongs: in the building,
  beside the `coating` room of the interior below.  (Today the engine
  refuses a placed item inside a building whose `envelope` is declared --
  the plot plan sees two items sharing a volume -- so that move needs the
  engine extended first; say so in your report.)

  SOLIDS ARE NOT PIPED.  A stream that carries only solids -- the bought
  powders, the spray-dried dispersion, the blends, the granules, the tablet
  cores -- is listed by the engine as "not routed: solids only, moved in
  containers or by conveyor", and a mixer or splitter all of whose streams
  are solids (the blenders, the compactor, the mill, the screen, the press)
  is not put on the rack.  What the router still draws: the solution, the
  gas loop, the solvent lines, the coating suspension and the coating air.
  The coating pan stays a junction (the suspension is piped to it), and the
  wet and coated tablets after it are listed as not routed because the
  coating dryer has no sized item -- they carry the coat's water, so they
  are not "solids only".  See the README (section 7).

  Grammar and checks: docs/design/a-plant-layout-is-declared-and-checked.md
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

items
