/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  THE GMP INTERIOR of the production building (DEV.md 4c C97: the wiring of
  phase B into this case).  The plot plan above sees the building as ONE box,
  the `productionBuilding` item -- its separations, its road access, its
  ignition; `envelope productionBuilding;` makes that box the SHELL of the
  rooms below, so every room must lie inside it (x -70..-20 m, y -18..18 m,
  z 0..10 m).  Grammar and checks: docs/ai/case-layout.md, "THE GMP
  INTERIOR"; record docs/design/a-gmp-interior-is-declared-and-checked.md.

  WHAT GRADE, AND WHY.  This is an ORAL SOLID DOSE (film-coated tablet)
  suite, not a sterile one.  EU GMP Annex 1, whose grade vocabulary A/B/C/D
  the engine speaks, is written for STERILE products; nothing in it applies
  to tablets by its own terms.  The rooms where product is exposed
  (dispensing, the granulation-and-compression train, coating, primary
  packaging, the corridor and airlocks that serve them, the IPC and wash
  rooms) are declared grade D BY ANALOGY, the usual practice for an OSD
  plant, and every other room CNC (controlled, not classified).  That is
  this case's statement, to be replaced by the company's own risk
  assessment -- not a value looked up.

  THE CASCADE.  Every pressure is declared to outside: CNC rooms +15 Pa,
  the clean corridor +35 Pa, gowning and the cascade airlocks between their
  neighbours, the personnel bubbles +45 Pa, the material sinks +5/+10 Pa
  (they draw air IN from both sides and exhaust it), the contained suite's
  own corridor +25 Pa and its process rooms +15 Pa, so air moves INTO the
  rooms where powder is open.  The step is Annex 1's guidance value,
  borrowed.  The technical floor is +5 Pa.

  CONTAINMENT.  The API is BOUGHT and its occupational exposure band is NOT
  KNOWN to this case.  Every room where the API is handled as an OPEN
  powder -- dispensing, blending, roller compaction, milling and screening,
  final blending, compression -- is declared contained, on the assumption
  that an anti-androgen is a potent compound, until the supplier's safety
  data sheet says otherwise: CONFIRM THE BAND (README section 9, question
  2).  A contained room is reached only through a bubble (people) or a sink
  (material, waste) airlock.  Coating and packaging handle tablets, not open
  powder, and are not contained -- revisit that if the band is high.

  THE FLOWS (one way each; nothing goes back through a room it left):
    * material in from the WAREHOUSE (south) to goods-in and the dispensary;
      the dispensed API and polymer leave EAST to the solution tank (the
      solvent area, outside), and the spray-dried dispersion comes back in
      through the east dock;
    * the PRODUCT runs east to west along the contained train (blending ->
      compaction -> milling -> final blending -> compression), out of the
      suite through a sink into the clean corridor, then coating ->
      packaging -> secondary packaging -> back SOUTH to the warehouse;
    * PEOPLE come in at the south lobby (street clothes), gown, and reach
      the work rooms from the clean corridor -- the contained suite through
      its own bubble airlock (over-garments) into its own corridor;
    * WASTE (press rejects, dust bags) leaves the contained suite by its
      north return corridor and a sink airlock to the waste room, never
      through a room the product crosses.
  The clean corridor carries people and closed containers of material both:
  declared `shared` below, with the reason.

  WHAT IS NOT IN ANY ROOM.  No placed item stands inside this building: the
  solid-dose machines are mass-balance placeholders with no size (README
  section 3), so `equipment ( )` lists nothing.  The coating air heater
  stands on the roof (z 10 m), above the technical floor.  The voids between
  the airlocks north of the clean corridor are service risers.

  EVERY POSITION, SIZE, GRADE AND PRESSURE HERE IS AN AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION
  for the group to replace with its own design; the ISPE Baseline Guide
  Volume 2 (Oral Solid Dosage Forms) is where a real OSD layout is argued,
  cited by title only.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
building
{
    name     "apalutamide OSD building";
    source   "author-set assumption for the group to replace with its own design; not a building design";
    reason   "the interior of the production building: where the tablets are dispensed, granulated, pressed, coated and packed";
    envelope productionBuilding;

    cascade
    {
        minimumStep 10 Pa;
        source "EU GMP Annex 1 (2022) para 4.14: a minimum of 10 Pa between adjacent rooms of different grades (guidance value) -- written for sterile products, borrowed here by analogy";
        reason "the guidance value, taken as the design step of an oral-solid-dose suite";
    }

    floors
    (
        { floor ground;    elevation 0 m;   height 5 m;   }
        { floor technical; elevation 5.5 m; height 4.5 m; }   // AHUs, utilities, switchgear
    );

    rooms
    (
        //  ---- the clean corridor and the personnel entrance (south) -------
        { room corridor;           floor ground; xMin -66 m; xMax -26 m; yMin -1 m;  yMax 3 m;   grade D;   pressure 35 Pa; relativeTo outside; }
        { room lobby;              floor ground; xMin -58 m; xMax -50 m; yMin -18 m; yMax -10 m; grade CNC; pressure 15 Pa; relativeTo outside;
          source "author-set"; reason "the staff entrance from the footpath along the warehouse: street clothes off, lockers"; }
        { room gowning;            floor ground; xMin -58 m; xMax -54 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -1 m;  grade D;   role gowning; regime cascade;
          pressure 25 Pa; relativeTo outside;
          source "author-set"; reason "factory garments on, a step-over bench, hands washed: CNC to grade D (Annex 1 para 4.12 (i), borrowed)"; }

        //  ---- receipt and dispensing (south-west, from the warehouse) ------
        { room goodsIn;            floor ground; xMin -70 m; xMax -58 m; yMin -18 m; yMax -10 m; grade CNC; pressure 15 Pa; relativeTo outside;
          source "author-set"; reason "released raw materials from the warehouse: outer packaging removed, containers wiped down"; }
        { room malIn;              floor ground; xMin -70 m; xMax -66 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -1 m;  grade D;   role materialAirlock; regime sink;
          pressure 5 Pa; relativeTo outside; }
        { room dispensing;         floor ground; xMin -66 m; xMax -58 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -4 m;  grade D;   pressure 20 Pa; relativeTo outside;
          containment yes; occupancy 2;
          source "author-set: the API's exposure band is NOT known -- confirm it from the supplier's safety data sheet";
          reason "every raw material weighed into kits under a downflow booth; the API is open here, so the room is contained until the band says otherwise"; }
        { room dispPAL;            floor ground; xMin -66 m; xMax -62 m; yMin -4 m;  yMax -1 m;  grade D;   role personnelAirlock; regime bubble;
          pressure 45 Pa; relativeTo outside; }
        { room dispOutMAL;         floor ground; xMin -62 m; xMax -58 m; yMin -4 m;  yMax -1 m;  grade D;   role materialAirlock; regime sink;
          pressure 10 Pa; relativeTo outside; }

        //  ---- support rooms off the corridor -------------------------------
        { room washRoom;           floor ground; xMin -54 m; xMax -49 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -1 m;  grade D;   pressure 25 Pa; relativeTo outside; occupancy 1; }
        { room ipcLab;             floor ground; xMin -49 m; xMax -45 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -1 m;  grade D;   pressure 35 Pa; relativeTo outside; occupancy 1;
          source "author-set"; reason "in-process control: tablet weight, hardness, thickness and friability beside the line"; }

        //  ---- coating and packaging (south-east), out to the warehouse ----
        { room coating;            floor ground; xMin -45 m; xMax -36 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -1 m;  grade D;   pressure 25 Pa; relativeTo outside; occupancy 1;
          source "author-set"; reason "the pan coater; below the corridor so its dust does not leave; not contained: it handles tablets, not open powder"; }
        { room packaging;          floor ground; xMin -36 m; xMax -26 m; yMin -7 m;  yMax -1 m;  grade D;   pressure 30 Pa; relativeTo outside; occupancy 3;
          source "author-set"; reason "primary packaging: the tablets into blisters"; }
        { room packMAL;            floor ground; xMin -36 m; xMax -26 m; yMin -10 m; yMax -7 m;  grade D;   role materialAirlock; regime cascade;
          pressure 20 Pa; relativeTo outside; }
        { room packagingMaterials; floor ground; xMin -50 m; xMax -36 m; yMin -18 m; yMax -10 m; grade CNC; pressure 15 Pa; relativeTo outside; }
        { room secondaryPackaging; floor ground; xMin -36 m; xMax -20 m; yMin -18 m; yMax -10 m; grade CNC; pressure 15 Pa; relativeTo outside; occupancy 2;
          source "author-set"; reason "blisters into cartons and cases, then back to the warehouse to await release"; }
        { room stairHall;          floor ground; xMin -26 m; xMax -20 m; yMin -10 m; yMax 3 m;   grade CNC; pressure 15 Pa; relativeTo outside; }

        //  ---- the contained suite (north) ----------------------------------
        { room suitePAL;           floor ground; xMin -54 m; xMax -50 m; yMin 3 m;   yMax 6 m;   grade D;   role personnelAirlock; regime bubble;
          pressure 45 Pa; relativeTo outside;
          source "author-set"; reason "over-garments and respiratory protection on, the bubble keeps the suite's dust in and the corridor's air out"; }
        { room suiteCorridor;      floor ground; xMin -58 m; xMax -40 m; yMin 6 m;   yMax 8.5 m; grade D;   pressure 25 Pa; relativeTo outside; containment yes; }
        { room compression;        floor ground; xMin -66 m; xMax -58 m; yMin 6 m;   yMax 15.5 m; grade D;  pressure 15 Pa; relativeTo outside; containment yes; occupancy 2; }
